IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc4-s84-definitions`

-- ccc4-s99-108-trafficking-and-others.l4 -- sections 99 to 108 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (PART III, Firearms and Other Weapons):
-- Trafficking Offences (99 to 101), Assembling Offence (102), Computer Data Offence (102.1), Export and Import Offences (103, 104),
-- Offence Relating to Altering Cartridge Magazine (104.1), Offences relating to Lost, Destroyed or Defaced Weapons, etc. (105 to 108).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone.  The conventions are those of ccc4-s85-98-use-possession.l4 (see its header and NOTES.md, fork F-OF):
--   an unmet element answers JUST FALSE; a case outside "without lawful excuse" or "otherwise than under the authority of" answers NOTHING;
--   the penalty subsection of each offence gives its class, its indictable limb and its summary limb (which takes the answer of section 787(1) as an input).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.

-- The minimum terms of ss 99(2), 100(2) and 103(2) and of s 102(2).  The core has constants for two, five, ten and fourteen years and for six months, not for these (NEEDS-CORE.md).
-- src:2172 | (a) in the case of a first offence, three years; and
-- src:2173 | (b) in the case of a second or subsequent offence, five years.
@ref s 99(2)(a) and (b), the minimum terms (src:2172-2173)
`s 99(2) three years` MEANS `Length of time` OF 3, 0, 0, FALSE

-- src:2199 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding ten years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of one year; or
@ref s 102(2)(a), the minimum term (src:2199)
`s 102(2) one year` MEANS `Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE

§ `Trafficking Offences`
§§ `Section 99 -- Weapons trafficking`

-- src:2166 | 99 (1) Every person commits an offence who
-- src:2167 | (a) manufactures or transfers, whether or not for consideration, or
-- src:2168 | (b) offers to do anything referred to in paragraph (a) in respect of
-- src:2169 | a prohibited firearm, a restricted firearm, a non-restricted firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, any ammunition or any prohibited ammunition knowing that the person is not authorized to do so under the Firearms Act or any other Act of Parliament or any regulations made under any Act of Parliament.
@ref s 99(1) (src:2166-2169)
GIVEN `the kind of thing` IS A `s 84(1) kind of thing`
      `the person manufactures it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 84(1) transfer: the person transfers it, whether or not for consideration` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person offers to manufacture or transfer it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that the person is not authorized to do so under the Firearms Act or any other Act of Parliament or any regulations made under any Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 99(1) the person commits an offence of weapons trafficking` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the elements` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the elements` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the answer of s 84(1) transfer is not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person commits an offence who (a) manufactures or transfers" (an unmet element)
    WHERE
        -- a prohibited firearm, a restricted firearm, a non-restricted firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, any ammunition or any prohibited ammunition
        `the thing is one that the subsection names` MEANS
               `s 84(1) the kind of thing is a firearm` `the kind of thing`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited weapon`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a restricted weapon`
               OR `s 84(1) the kind of thing is a prohibited device` `the kind of thing`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a firearm part`
               OR `s 84(1) the kind of thing is ammunition or prohibited ammunition` `the kind of thing`
        -- (a) manufactures or transfers, whether or not for consideration, or (b) offers to do anything referred to in paragraph (a)
        `the conduct` MEANS `s 84(1) some limb holds` (LIST (JUST `the person manufactures it`), `s 84(1) transfer: the person transfers it, whether or not for consideration`, (JUST `the person offers to manufacture or transfer it`))
        `the elements` MEANS `s 84(1) every condition of the limb holds` (LIST (JUST `the thing is one that the subsection names`), `the conduct`, (JUST `the person knows that the person is not authorized to do so under the Firearms Act or any other Act of Parliament or any regulations made under any Act of Parliament`))

-- src:2170 | Punishment — firearm
-- src:2171 | (2) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1) when the object in question is a prohibited firearm, a restricted firearm, a non-restricted firearm, a prohibited device, a firearm part, any ammunition or any prohibited ammunition is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 14 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of
-- src:2172 | (a) in the case of a first offence, three years; and
-- src:2173 | (b) in the case of a second or subsequent offence, five years.
@ref s 99(2) (src:2170-2173)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 99(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 99(2) (src:2170-2173)
GIVEN `the kind of thing the object in question is` IS A `s 84(1) kind of thing`
      `it is a second or subsequent offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Punishment
`s 99(2) the punishment when the object in question is a firearm, device, part or ammunition` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the object is one the subsection names`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "when the object in question is" (subsection (3) governs any other case)
        IF `it is a second or subsequent offence` THEN JUST (Punishment WITH `mode` IS `by indictment`, `maximum imprisonment` IS (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`), `minimum imprisonment` IS (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`), `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`, `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`)   -- (b) in the case of a second or subsequent offence, five years
        OTHERWISE JUST (Punishment WITH `mode` IS `by indictment`, `maximum imprisonment` IS (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`), `minimum imprisonment` IS (`imprisonment for a term of` `s 99(2) three years`), `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`, `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`)   -- (a) in the case of a first offence, three years
    WHERE
        `the object is one the subsection names` MEANS
               `s 84(1) the kind of thing is a firearm` `the kind of thing the object in question is`
               OR `s 84(1) the kind of thing is a prohibited device` `the kind of thing the object in question is`
               OR `the kind of thing the object in question is` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a firearm part`
               OR `s 84(1) the kind of thing is ammunition or prohibited ammunition` `the kind of thing the object in question is`

-- src:2174 | Punishment — other cases
-- src:2175 | (3) In any other case, a person who commits an offence under subsection (1) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years.
@ref s 99(3) (src:2174-2175)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 99(3) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 99(3) (src:2174-2175)
GIVEN `the kind of thing the object in question is` IS A `s 84(1) kind of thing`
GIVETH A MAYBE Punishment
`s 99(3) the punishment in any other case` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the case is one subsection (2) governs`) THEN JUST (Punishment WITH `mode` IS `by indictment`, `maximum imprisonment` IS (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`), `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`, `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`, `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In any other case" (subsection (2) governs when the object is a firearm, device, part or ammunition)
    WHERE
        `the case is one subsection (2) governs` MEANS
               `s 84(1) the kind of thing is a firearm` `the kind of thing the object in question is`
               OR `s 84(1) the kind of thing is a prohibited device` `the kind of thing the object in question is`
               OR `the kind of thing the object in question is` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a firearm part`
               OR `s 84(1) the kind of thing is ammunition or prohibited ammunition` `the kind of thing the object in question is`

§§ `Section 100 -- Possession for purpose of weapons trafficking`

-- src:2177 | 100 (1) Every person commits an offence who possesses a prohibited firearm, a restricted firearm, a non-restricted firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, any ammunition or any prohibited ammunition for the purpose of
-- src:2178 | (a) transferring it, whether or not for consideration, or
-- src:2179 | (b) offering to transfer it,
-- src:2180 | knowing that the person is not authorized to transfer it under the Firearms Act or any other Act of Parliament or any regulations made under any Act of Parliament.
@ref s 100(1) (src:2177-2180)
GIVEN `the kind of thing` IS A `s 84(1) kind of thing`
      `the person possesses it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 84(1) transfer: the person possesses it for the purpose of transferring it, whether or not for consideration` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person possesses it for the purpose of offering to transfer it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that the person is not authorized to transfer it under the Firearms Act or any other Act of Parliament or any regulations made under any Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 100(1) the person commits an offence of possession for the purpose of weapons trafficking` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the elements` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the elements` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the answer of s 84(1) transfer is not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person commits an offence who possesses a prohibited firearm" (an unmet element)
    WHERE
        -- a prohibited firearm, a restricted firearm, a non-restricted firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, any ammunition or any prohibited ammunition
        `the thing is one that the subsection names` MEANS
               `s 84(1) the kind of thing is a firearm` `the kind of thing`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited weapon`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a restricted weapon`
               OR `s 84(1) the kind of thing is a prohibited device` `the kind of thing`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a firearm part`
               OR `s 84(1) the kind of thing is ammunition or prohibited ammunition` `the kind of thing`
        -- for the purpose of (a) transferring it, whether or not for consideration, or (b) offering to transfer it
        `the purpose` MEANS `s 84(1) some limb holds` (LIST `s 84(1) transfer: the person possesses it for the purpose of transferring it, whether or not for consideration`, (JUST `the person possesses it for the purpose of offering to transfer it`))
        `the elements` MEANS `s 84(1) every condition of the limb holds` (LIST (JUST `the thing is one that the subsection names`), (JUST `the person possesses it`), `the purpose`, (JUST `the person knows that the person is not authorized to transfer it under the Firearms Act or any other Act of Parliament or any regulations made under any Act of Parliament`))

