§§ `Section 101 -- Transfer without authority`

-- src:2187 | Transfer without authority
-- src:2188 | 101 (1) Every person commits an offence who transfers a prohibited firearm, a restricted firearm, a non-restricted firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, any ammunition or any prohibited ammunition to any person otherwise than under the authority of the Firearms Act or any other Act of Parliament or any regulations made under an Act of Parliament.
@ref s 101(1) (src:2187-2188)
GIVEN `the kind of thing` IS A `s 84(1) kind of thing`
      `s 84(1) transfer: the person transfers it to any person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is under the authority of the Firearms Act or any other Act of Parliament or any regulations made under an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 101(1) the person commits an offence of transfer without authority` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 84(1) transfer: the person transfers it to any person` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR NOT (`the thing is one that the subsection names`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person commits an offence who transfers a prohibited firearm" (an unmet element)
        IF `s 84(1) transfer: the person transfers it to any person` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the answer of s 84(1) transfer is not covered
        IF `the transfer is under the authority of the Firearms Act or any other Act of Parliament or any regulations made under an Act of Parliament` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "otherwise than under the authority of"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        -- a prohibited firearm, a restricted firearm, a non-restricted firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, any ammunition or any prohibited ammunition
        `the thing is one that the subsection names` MEANS
               `s 84(1) the kind of thing is a firearm` `the kind of thing`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited weapon`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a restricted weapon`
               OR `s 84(1) the kind of thing is a prohibited device` `the kind of thing`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a firearm part`
               OR `s 84(1) the kind of thing is ammunition or prohibited ammunition` `the kind of thing`

-- src:2189 | Punishment
-- src:2190 | (2) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1)
-- src:2191 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years; or
-- src:2192 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 101(2) (src:2189-2192)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 101(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 101(2)(a) (src:2189-2192)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 101(2)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment WITH
            `mode` IS `by indictment`
            `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`
            `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
            `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
            `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`

@ref s 101(2)(b) (src:2192)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 101(2)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- the section states no penalty for this limb: the seam takes the answer of section 787(1), which another part encodes
§ `Assembling Offence`

§§ `Section 102 -- Making automatic firearm`

-- src:2195 | Making automatic firearm
-- src:2196 | 102 (1) Every person commits an offence who, without lawful excuse, alters a firearm so that it is capable of, or manufactures or assembles any firearm that is capable of, discharging projectiles in rapid succession during one pressure of the trigger.
@ref s 102(1) (src:2195-2196)
GIVEN `the person alters a firearm so that it is capable of discharging projectiles in rapid succession during one pressure of the trigger` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person manufactures or assembles a firearm that is capable of discharging projectiles in rapid succession during one pressure of the trigger` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 102(1) the person commits an offence of making an automatic firearm` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person alters a firearm so that it is capable of discharging projectiles in rapid succession during one pressure of the trigger` OR `the person manufactures or assembles a firearm that is capable of discharging projectiles in rapid succession during one pressure of the trigger`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person commits an offence who, without lawful excuse, alters a firearm so that it is capable of" (an unmet element)
        IF `the person has a lawful excuse` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without lawful excuse"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:2197 | Punishment
-- src:2198 | (2) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1)
-- src:2199 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding ten years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of one year; or
-- src:2200 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 102(2) (src:2197-2200)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 102(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 102(2)(a) (src:2197-2200)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 102(2)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment WITH
            `mode` IS `by indictment`
            `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`
            `minimum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `s 102(2) one year`
            `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
            `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`

@ref s 102(2)(b) (src:2200)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 102(2)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- the section states no penalty for this limb: the seam takes the answer of section 787(1), which another part encodes
§ `Computer Data Offence`

§§ `Section 102.1 -- Possession of computer data`

-- In this section, computer data and computer system have the same meaning as in subsection 342.1(2): the answers of the part that encodes that subsection are inputs.
-- src:2211 | Definitions of computer data and computer system
-- src:2212 | (4) In this section, computer data and computer system have the same meaning as in subsection 342.1(2).
@ref s 102.1(4) "computer data" (src:2211-2212)
GIVEN `s 342.1(2) the thing is computer data` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 102.1(4) computer data` MEANS `s 342.1(2) the thing is computer data`   -- "computer data ... have the same meaning as in subsection 342.1(2)": the answer of that subsection is the answer here

-- src:2211 | Definitions of computer data and computer system
-- src:2212 | (4) In this section, computer data and computer system have the same meaning as in subsection 342.1(2).
@ref s 102.1(4) "computer system" (src:2211-2212)
GIVEN `s 342.1(2) the thing is a computer system` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 102.1(4) computer system` MEANS `s 342.1(2) the thing is a computer system`   -- "computer system ... have the same meaning as in subsection 342.1(2)": the answer of that subsection is the answer here

-- src:2203 | Possession of computer data
-- src:2204 | 102.1 (1) Every person commits an offence who possesses or accesses computer data that pertain to a firearm — other than a firearm that is deemed under subsection 84(3) not to be a firearm — or a prohibited device and that are capable of being used with a 3D printer, metal milling machine or similar computer system for the purpose of manufacturing or trafficking a firearm or prohibited device derived from that computer data otherwise than under the authority of the Firearms Act or any other Act of Parliament or any regulations made under an Act of Parliament.
@ref s 102.1(1) (src:2203-2204)
GIVEN `s 102.1(4) computer data: the thing is computer data` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person possesses or accesses it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data pertain to a firearm other than a firearm that is deemed under subsection 84(3) not to be a firearm, or to a prohibited device` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data are capable of being used with a 3D printer, metal milling machine or similar computer system for the purpose of manufacturing or trafficking a firearm or prohibited device derived from that computer data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts under the authority of the Firearms Act or any other Act of Parliament or any regulations made under an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 102.1(1) the person commits an offence of possession of computer data` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person possesses or accesses it` AND `the data pertain to a firearm other than a firearm that is deemed under subsection 84(3) not to be a firearm, or to a prohibited device` AND `the data are capable of being used with a 3D printer, metal milling machine or similar computer system for the purpose of manufacturing or trafficking a firearm or prohibited device derived from that computer data`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person commits an offence who possesses or accesses computer data that pertain to a firearm" (an unmet element)
        IF `s 102.1(4) computer data: the thing is computer data` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "computer data and computer system have the same meaning as in subsection 342.1(2)" (what is not computer data is not within the subsection)
        IF `s 102.1(4) computer data: the thing is computer data` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer of s 342.1(2) is not covered
        IF `the person acts under the authority of the Firearms Act or any other Act of Parliament or any regulations made under an Act of Parliament` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "otherwise than under the authority of"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:2205 | Distribution of computer data
-- src:2206 | (2) Every person commits an offence who distributes, publishes or makes available computer data that pertain to a firearm — other than a firearm that is deemed under subsection 84(3) not to be a firearm — or a prohibited device and that are capable of being used with a 3D printer, metal milling machine or similar computer system knowing that the computer data are intended to be used for the purpose of manufacturing or trafficking a firearm or prohibited device derived from that computer data otherwise than under the authority of the Firearms Act or any other Act of Parliament or any regulations made under an Act of Parliament.
@ref s 102.1(2) (src:2205-2206)
GIVEN `s 102.1(4) computer data: the thing is computer data` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person distributes, publishes or makes it available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data pertain to a firearm other than a firearm that is deemed under subsection 84(3) not to be a firearm, or to a prohibited device` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data are capable of being used with a 3D printer, metal milling machine or similar computer system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that the data are intended to be used for the purpose of manufacturing or trafficking a firearm or prohibited device derived from that computer data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts under the authority of the Firearms Act or any other Act of Parliament or any regulations made under an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 102.1(2) the person commits an offence of distribution of computer data` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person distributes, publishes or makes it available` AND `the data pertain to a firearm other than a firearm that is deemed under subsection 84(3) not to be a firearm, or to a prohibited device` AND `the data are capable of being used with a 3D printer, metal milling machine or similar computer system` AND `the person knows that the data are intended to be used for the purpose of manufacturing or trafficking a firearm or prohibited device derived from that computer data`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person commits an offence who distributes, publishes or makes available computer data" (an unmet element)
        IF `s 102.1(4) computer data: the thing is computer data` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "computer data and computer system have the same meaning as in subsection 342.1(2)" (what is not computer data is not within the subsection)
        IF `s 102.1(4) computer data: the thing is computer data` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer of s 342.1(2) is not covered
        IF `the person acts under the authority of the Firearms Act or any other Act of Parliament or any regulations made under an Act of Parliament` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "otherwise than under the authority of"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

