§§ `Section 107 -- False statements`

-- src:2264 | False statements
-- src:2265 | 107 (1) Every person commits an offence who knowingly makes, before a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer, a false report or statement concerning the loss, theft or destruction of a prohibited firearm, a restricted firearm, a non-restricted firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, any prohibited ammunition, an authorization, a licence or a registration certificate.
@ref s 107(1) (src:2264-2265)
GIVEN `the kind of thing` IS A `s 84(1) kind of thing`
      `it is an authorization, a licence or a registration certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person makes a report or statement before a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report or statement concerns the loss, theft or destruction of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report or statement is false` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person makes it knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 107(1) the person commits an offence by making a false report or statement` MEANS
    IF     (`the thing is one that the subsection names`)
       AND `the person makes a report or statement before a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer`
       AND `the report or statement concerns the loss, theft or destruction of it`
       AND `the report or statement is false`
       AND `the person makes it knowingly`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person commits an offence who knowingly makes, before a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer, a false report or statement" (an unmet element)
    WHERE
        -- a prohibited firearm, a restricted firearm, a non-restricted firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, any prohibited ammunition, an authorization, a licence or a registration certificate
        `the thing is one that the subsection names` MEANS
               `s 84(1) the kind of thing is a firearm` `the kind of thing`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited weapon`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a restricted weapon`
               OR `s 84(1) the kind of thing is a prohibited device` `the kind of thing`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: prohibited ammunition`
               OR `it is an authorization, a licence or a registration certificate`

-- src:2266 | Punishment
-- src:2267 | (2) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1)
-- src:2268 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years; or
-- src:2269 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 107(2) (src:2266-2269)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 107(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 107(2)(a) (src:2266-2269)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 107(2)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment WITH
            `mode` IS `by indictment`
            `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`
            `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
            `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
            `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`

@ref s 107(2)(b) (src:2269)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 107(2)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- the section states no penalty for this limb: the seam takes the answer of section 787(1), which another part encodes
-- src:2270 | Definition of report or statement
-- src:2271 | (3) In this section, report or statement means an assertion of fact, opinion, belief or knowledge, whether material or not and whether admissible or not.
@ref s 107(3) (src:2270-2271)
DECLARE `s 107(3) assertion` IS ONE OF
    `s 107(3) assertion: of fact`
    `s 107(3) assertion: of opinion`
    `s 107(3) assertion: of belief`
    `s 107(3) assertion: of knowledge`
    `s 107(3) assertion: a thing that is none of those`

@ref s 107(3) (src:2270-2271)
GIVEN `the assertion` IS A `s 107(3) assertion`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 107(3) report or statement` MEANS
    IF `the assertion` EQUALS `s 107(3) assertion: a thing that is none of those`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "report or statement means an assertion of fact, opinion, belief or knowledge" (whether material or not and whether admissible or not makes no difference)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `Section 108 -- Tampering with serial number`

-- src:2272 | Tampering with serial number
-- src:2273 | 108 (1) Every person commits an offence who, without lawful excuse,
-- src:2274 | (a) alters, defaces or removes a serial number on a firearm; or
-- src:2275 | (b) possesses a firearm knowing that the serial number on it has been altered, defaced or removed.
@ref s 108(1) (src:2272-2275)
GIVEN `the kind of thing` IS A `s 84(1) kind of thing`
      `the person alters, defaces or removes a serial number on it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person possesses it knowing that the serial number on it has been altered, defaced or removed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 108(1) the person commits an offence of tampering with a serial number` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 84(1) the kind of thing is a firearm` `the kind of thing` AND (`the person alters, defaces or removes a serial number on it` OR `the person possesses it knowing that the serial number on it has been altered, defaced or removed`)) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person commits an offence who, without lawful excuse, ... alters, defaces or removes a serial number on a firearm" (an unmet element)
        IF `the person has a lawful excuse` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without lawful excuse"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:2276 | Punishment
-- src:2277 | (2) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1)
-- src:2278 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years; or
-- src:2279 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 108(2) (src:2276-2279)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 108(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 108(2)(a) (src:2276-2279)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 108(2)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment WITH
            `mode` IS `by indictment`
            `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`
            `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
            `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
            `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`

@ref s 108(2)(b) (src:2279)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 108(2)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- the section states no penalty for this limb: the seam takes the answer of section 787(1), which another part encodes
-- src:2280 | Exception
-- src:2281 | (3) No person is guilty of an offence under paragraph (1)(b) by reason only of possessing a prohibited firearm or restricted firearm the serial number on which has been altered, defaced or removed, if that serial number has been replaced and a registration certificate in respect of the firearm has been issued setting out a new serial number for the firearm.
@ref s 108(3) (src:2280-2281)
GIVEN `the kind of thing` IS A `s 84(1) kind of thing`
      `the serial number has been replaced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a registration certificate in respect of the firearm has been issued setting out a new serial number for the firearm` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 108(3) no person is guilty of an offence under paragraph (1)(b) by reason only of possessing the firearm` MEANS
    IF     (`the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a restricted firearm`)
       AND `the serial number has been replaced`
       AND `a registration certificate in respect of the firearm has been issued setting out a new serial number for the firearm`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No person is guilty of an offence under paragraph (1)(b) by reason only of possessing a prohibited firearm or restricted firearm" whose serial number has been replaced and for which a registration certificate setting out the new number has been issued (it says nothing of any other case)

-- src:2282 | Evidence
-- src:2283 | (4) In proceedings for an offence under subsection (1), evidence that a person possesses a firearm the serial number on which has been wholly or partially obliterated otherwise than through normal use over time is, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, proof that the person possesses the firearm knowing that the serial number on it has been altered, defaced or removed.
@ref s 108(4) (src:2282-2283)
GIVEN `the person possesses the firearm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the serial number on it has been wholly or partially obliterated otherwise than through normal use over time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 108(4) the evidence is proof that the person possesses the firearm knowing that the serial number on it has been altered, defaced or removed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person possesses the firearm` AND `the serial number on it has been wholly or partially obliterated otherwise than through normal use over time`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "evidence that a person possesses a firearm the serial number on which has been wholly or partially obliterated otherwise than through normal use over time"
        IF `there is evidence to the contrary` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of evidence to the contrary" (the rule of proof applies only in the absence of evidence to the contrary)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `The duties of sections 105 and 106, as regulative rules`

-- Sections 105(1) and 106(1) make it an offence not to do something "with reasonable despatch"; read as duties of the person who lost, found or destroyed the thing.
-- The text fixes no period ("with reasonable despatch"), so the rules carry no WITHIN (a deadline the text does not state is not invented; fork F-despatch): a trace that does not contain the act leaves the duty standing.
-- The person bound is the person in the seat (the core's `the accused`: the individual charged, or liable to be charged).
-- The decision-function twins of these rules are `s 105(1)(a) ...`, `s 105(1)(b) ...` and `s 106(1) ...` above.
-- src:2247 | Losing or finding
-- src:2248 | 105 (1) Every person commits an offence who
-- src:2249 | (a) having lost a prohibited firearm, a restricted firearm, a non-restricted firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, any prohibited ammunition, an authorization, a licence or a registration certificate, or having had it stolen from the person’s possession, does not with reasonable despatch report the loss to a peace officer, to a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer; or
@ref s 105(1)(a), the duty (src:2247-2249)
DECLARE `s 105 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 105 report the loss to a peace officer, to a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer`
    `s 105 deliver the found thing to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer, or report the finding to one of them`
    `s 106 report the destruction to a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer`

@ref s 105(1)(a) (src:2247-2249)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 105 act`
`s 105(1)(a) the duty to report a loss` MEANS
    PARTY `the accused`
    MUST `s 105 report the loss to a peace officer, to a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer`

-- src:2250 | (b) on finding a prohibited firearm, a restricted firearm, a non-restricted firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device or any prohibited ammunition that the person has reasonable grounds to believe has been lost or abandoned, does not with reasonable despatch deliver it to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer or report the finding to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer.
@ref s 105(1)(b), the duty (src:2250)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 105 act`
`s 105(1)(b) the duty to deliver or report a find` MEANS
    PARTY `the accused`
    MUST `s 105 deliver the found thing to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer, or report the finding to one of them`

-- src:2255 | Destroying
-- src:2256 | 106 (1) Every person commits an offence who
-- src:2257 | (a) after destroying any prohibited firearm, restricted firearm, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device or prohibited ammunition, or
-- src:2258 | (b) on becoming aware of the destruction of any prohibited firearm, restricted firearm, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device or prohibited ammunition that was in the person’s possession before its destruction,
-- src:2259 | does not with reasonable despatch report the destruction to a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer.
@ref s 106(1), the duty (src:2255-2259)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 105 act`
`s 106(1) the duty to report a destruction` MEANS
    PARTY `the accused`
    MUST `s 106 report the destruction to a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer`

